'''León''' ([[Baliscano]] meaning "lion", {{Langx|mxi|لِييُونْ|Liyún}}) is a [[Planned communities in Balisca|planned]] {{W|satellite city}} under active development in the [[Araucaria|Araucarian region]] of [[Tukupi]]. It is located in the northwestern [[Alpujarra]], on the banks of the [[Coroado river]]. The [[León Company|Compañía León]] [[W:Cooperative federation|cooperative federation]] started developing the area in the 1950s and development has continued at steady pace since then. The commune had a population of 311,647 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. 

As a result of growth of the [[Castejón Metropolis]], León is now considered to be a {{W|satellite city}} of the metropolis, and is included in the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]]. 

